{{Quote|You were loyal to both your bosses. Would you be loyal to me if I were to spare you?|Boba Fett to the Gamorrean|<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" />}}
A [[Gamorrean]] '''guard''' served under [[crime lord]]s [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] and [[Bib Fortuna]] before the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]] [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|took over]] [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] and established his own [[Fett gotra|gotra]]. Sometime after the attack, the Gamorrean and a [[Unidentified Gamorrean guard 2|fellow guard]] were captured and brought before Fett. Refusing to [[torture]] the Gamorreans, Fett allowed them both to live as long as they pledged their loyalty to him.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" />

As Fett's guard, the Gamorrean wore a [[metal]] [[helmet]] and a [[pauldron]] on each shoulder, whereas the other guard wore only a single pauldron. They carried a small [[sword]] for melee combat and a [[Gamorrean war ax|Gamorrean battle-ax]]. When Fett was [[Ambush outside of the Sanctuary|ambushed]] by the [[Order of the Night Wind]] in [[Mos Espa]], the helmeted Gamorrean sprang into action and broke through the [[assassin]]s' defenses. Along with the other guard, the Gamorrean dragged Fett back to the palace's [[Bacta tank|bacta pod]] to heal from wounds sustained in the battle.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> After a failed assassination [[Assassination attempt on Boba Fett|attempt]], Boba put the guard in his [[Bacta tank]], after being bitten by [[Krrsantan]] in the left shoulder.<ref name="Streets">{{BOBF|Chapter 3: The Streets of Mos Espa}}</ref>

Later, guard participates with their comrade in the [[Battle of Mos Espa|Battle for Mos Espa]] against the Pyke Syndicate and unfortunately they are killed by the [[Klatooinian]]s when the three crime families betray Boba and join the Pykes. The Klatooinians pushed them of a cliff to theirs deaths.<ref name="Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Gamorrean guard first appeared in "[[Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land]]," the premiere episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'',<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> which released on [[Disney+]] on [[December 29]], [[2021]].<ref name="Disney+ Premiere">{{DisneyPlusYouTube|t9Ca4ARSfqA|Next On Disney+ &#124; December 2021}}</ref> The guard was played by [[Frank Trigg]], who is also a former mixed martial artist, color commentator, pro wrestler, MMA referre, and TV host.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" />

